TITLE: Qube attributes

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2P-CONFIG-010
TITLE: Qube property configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall set each qube property named in the desired state to
the value given there.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesTools, Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-STATE
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_property_set

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2P-CONFIG-020
TITLE: Property reset to default
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall restore a qube property to its default value on
request.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesTools, Terraform
RATIONALE: >>>
A property holding its default is not the same state as a property explicitly
set to the same value, because the default tracks later system changes.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-STATE
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_property_reset

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2P-CONFIG-030
TITLE: Qube feature configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall bring a qube's features to the set of values given in
the desired state.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesTools, Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-STATE
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_feature_set

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2P-CONFIG-040
TITLE: Qube service configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall set a named qube service to enabled or disabled
through its corresponding service feature.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesTools, Terraform
RATIONALE: >>>
Services have no storage of their own; a service is the feature named
``service.<name>``, so the two views must not diverge.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-STATE
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_feature_set

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2P-CONFIG-050
TITLE: Qube tag configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall bring a qube's tag set to the tags given in the
desired state.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesTools, Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-STATE
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_tag_set
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_tag_remove

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2P-CONFIG-060
TITLE: Qube notes
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall set the free-form notes attached to a qube.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesTools, Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-STATE
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_notes_set

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2P-CONFIG-070
TITLE: Notes size limit
STATEMENT: >>>
If notes exceed 256 000 bytes, then the management tool shall reject the
change and leave the stored notes untouched.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Unwanted-behaviour
PRODUCT: Ansible, QubesTools, Terraform
RATIONALE: >>>
Notes are qube-visible text held in dom0, so the Admin API caps them at 256 000 bytes.
Scoped to the components that expose notes; the wider gap is carried by
L2P-CONFIG-060.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-STATE
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ISOLATION
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_notes_set

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2P-CONFIG-080
TITLE: Qube class immutability
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall reject a request to change the class of an existing
qube.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesTools, Terraform
RATIONALE: >>>
Class fixes a qube's storage layout and startup semantics at creation, so a
declared class change is a request to recreate, never to mutate.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-STATE
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_create

