[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Device assignment

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2P-DEVICE-010
TITLE: Transient device attachment
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall attach a device to a qube for the lifetime of that
qube's current run.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Salt, QubesTools
RATIONALE: >>>
An attachment does not survive a restart, so it is an operation rather than
declarable state; the Ansible collection deliberately manages assignments only.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-OPERATE
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ADMINAPI
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_device_attach

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2P-DEVICE-020
TITLE: Persistent device assignment
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall assign a device to a qube so that the assignment
survives a restart of that qube.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesTools, Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-STATE
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_device_assign

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2P-DEVICE-030
TITLE: Device assignment modes
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall set a device assignment's mode to ask-to-attach,
auto-attach or required.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesTools, Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-STATE
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_device_set_required

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2P-DEVICE-040
TITLE: PCI assignment constraint
STATEMENT: >>>
If a PCI device is bound to a qube, then the management tool shall record it as
a required assignment rather than an attachment.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Unwanted-behaviour
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesTools, Terraform
RATIONALE: >>>
PCI passthrough is fixed at qube start, so any weaker binding leaves the qube
running without the device it was configured to have.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-STATE
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_device_assign

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Network and firewall

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2P-NET-010
TITLE: Netvm validation
STATEMENT: >>>
If the qube named as netvm does not provide network, then the management tool
shall reject the change.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Unwanted-behaviour
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesTools, Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-STATE
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_property_set

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2P-NET-020
TITLE: Firewall rule set
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall apply an ordered set of firewall rules to a qube,
replacing the rules previously in force.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesTools, Terraform
RATIONALE: >>>
Rules are evaluated in order and the first match wins, so a rule set is only
meaningful as a whole sequence.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-STATE
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_firewall_set

