[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Drift and recovery

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2P-CONV-060
TITLE: Drift detection
STATEMENT: >>>
When a managed object's live configuration differs from the recorded state, the management tool
shall report that difference in the change preview.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Event-driven
PRODUCT: Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-RECONCILE
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-OBSERVABILITY
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2P-CONV-070
TITLE: Drift correction
STATEMENT: >>>
When a managed qube was changed or removed outside the tool, the management tool shall restore its
declared state on the next run.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Event-driven
PRODUCT: Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-RECONCILE
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2P-CONV-080
TITLE: Failed-creation rollback
STATEMENT: >>>
If creating a qube fails, then the management tool shall remove only objects that the failed run
itself created.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Unwanted-behaviour
PRODUCT: Terraform
RATIONALE: >>>
A rollback that deletes a pre-existing qube destroys data the run never owned.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-RECONCILE
  ROLE: Refines

